=== Independent agencies ===

Several state-owned enterprises and regulatory bodies operate under the authority of the government but with varying degrees of independence from ministerial control:

* The [[Balboa Canal Authority]] operates under the [[Ministry of Interior (Balboa)|Ministry of Interior]] and is responsible for the sovereign governance of the [[Balboa Canal]], including transit policy, toll rates, and compliance with the [[Treaty of Areza]].
* The [[Bank of Balboa]] is the central bank, responsible for monetary policy, banking supervision, and serving as fiscal agent for government debt issuance. The bank operates with operational independence from the executive branch, though its governor is appointed by the president.
* The [[Balboa Financial Services Authority]] regulates financial markets, securities trading, and the insurance sector. It operates independently of the Ministry of Finance in its supervisory functions.
* The [[National Anti-Discrimination Tribunal]] is an independent judicial body with jurisdiction over discrimination cases arising under the [[Twelve Guarantees]]. It operates separately from the regular court system and maintains four regional offices.

== Legislative branch ==

{{main|National Assembly of Balboa}}

The National Assembly ({{lang|ca|Assemblea Nacional}}) is the unicameral legislature of the Republic of Balboa, consisting of 120 members elected by {{w|single transferable vote}} (STV) from multi-member constituencies corresponding to the five provinces. There is no electoral threshold, allowing small parties and regional movements to win representation.

The Assembly operates on a system of {{w|staggered elections}}: half of the seats (60) are contested every two years, with each member serving a four-year term. The Assembly is divided into two classes — Class A and Class B — each of 60 members, elected in alternating years. This system provides continuity while ensuring regular electoral accountability, but also means that the president's political mandate and the Assembly's composition may diverge, as presidential elections (every five years) and Assembly elections (every two years) operate on different cycles.

The [[Third Guarantee]] of the [[Twelve Guarantees]] requires that a minimum number of seats in the Assembly be allocated to representatives of the former [[International Mandate of Sant Cristòfor|mandate territory]], ensuring that the Black and mixed populations of the Sant Cristòfor region have guaranteed representation regardless of provincial electoral outcomes. The minimum seat allocation is set within the overall 120-seat total and is adjusted by the Constitutional Court following each census.

=== Powers of the National Assembly ===

The Assembly's powers include:

* Enacting legislation
* Approving the national budget
* Confirming presidential cabinet appointments
* Overriding presidential vetoes by a three-fifths majority
* Authorising the domestic deployment of the armed forces
* Impeaching the president by a two-thirds majority
* Calling [[snap elections]] with a three-fifths vote of no confidence

Legislation may be introduced by the president, by individual Assembly members, or by Assembly committees. Bills must pass the Assembly by a simple majority of those present and voting, subject to the quorum requirement of a majority of all members. The president has ten days to sign or veto a bill; a veto may be overridden by a three-fifths majority of the full Assembly.

== Judicial branch ==

{{main|Judiciary of Balboa|Constitutional Court of Balboa|Supreme Court of Balboa}}

The Balboan judiciary is a three-tier system consisting of courts of first instance, the Supreme Court, and the Constitutional Court. The judiciary operates independently of the executive and legislative branches, in accordance with the constitution and the [[Twelve Guarantees]].

=== Courts of first instance ===

Courts of first instance are the trial courts with general jurisdiction over civil, criminal, and administrative matters. They are organised by province and sit in each comarca. Judges are appointed by the Ministry of Justice from among qualified legal practitioners, subject to a competitive examination process. First-instance rulings may be appealed to the Supreme Court.

=== Supreme Court ===

The Supreme Court of Balboa ({{lang|ca|Tribunal Suprem}}) is the court of final appeal for all non-constitutional matters, including civil, criminal, and commercial cases. The Supreme Court is seated in [[Sant Bart]] and consists of a Chief Justice and twelve associate justices, appointed for non-renewable fifteen-year terms. Justices are appointed by the president from a list of candidates prepared by the Judicial Council, an independent body of senior judges and legal scholars.

=== Constitutional Court ===

The Constitutional Court of Balboa ({{lang|ca|Tribunal Constitucional}}) has exclusive jurisdiction over constitutional questions, including the interpretation and enforcement of the [[Twelve Guarantees]]. The court consists of nine justices appointed for non-renewable twelve-year terms. Three justices are appointed by the president, three by the National Assembly, and three by the Supreme Court from among its own members. The Constitutional Court has the power of {{w|judicial review}} and may strike down legislation or executive actions that violate the constitution, including the Guarantees.

Under the [[Twelfth Guarantee]], the [[AC Tribunal]] in the [[International City of Areza]] has jurisdiction over disputes concerning the interpretation and enforcement of the Twelve Guarantees. The Balboan Constitutional Court hears Guarantees cases at first instance, but its rulings may be appealed to the AC Tribunal, which has the final authority on Guarantees matters. The AC Tribunal may also take direct jurisdiction in cases involving serious or systematic violations of the Guarantees, bypassing the domestic courts.

=== National Anti-Discrimination Tribunal ===

The [[National Anti-Discrimination Tribunal]] is a specialised judicial body with jurisdiction over discrimination cases arising under the Guarantees. It operates separately from the regular court system and maintains four regional offices, covering Tramuntana and Nurra, Jala, Estret, and Migjorn. The Tribunal's rulings may be appealed to the Supreme Court.

== Security and defence ==

{{main|Balboan Defence Forces|National Police force of Balboa}}

The Balboan Defence Forces (BDF; {{lang|ca|Forces Armades de Balboa}}, FAB) are the professional military forces of the Republic, consisting of approximately 30,000 active personnel in two branches: the [[Balboan Army|Army]] and the [[Balboan Naval and Air Service|Naval and Air Service]] (which includes the [[Balboan Coast Guard|Coast Guard]] and the [[Balboan Air Wing|Air Wing]]). The [[President of Balboa]] serves as commander-in-chief, with the civilian [[Minister of Defence (Balboa)|Minister of Defence]] exercising day-to-day administrative oversight through the [[Ministry of Defence (Balboa)|Ministry of Defence]]. The BDF's primary mission is the defence of the [[Balboa Canal]] and the country's territorial integrity; it also provides support to civilian law enforcement and to the [[International Cooperative Police Force]] in the event of a security emergency.

The [[National Police force of Balboa|National Police Force]] ({{lang|ca|Força Nacional de Policia}}) is the civilian law enforcement agency, separate from the BDF. It operates with approximately 70,000 officers (a ratio of 1:500) and is responsible for general policing, border control, traffic enforcement, and criminal investigation. The police force was established following the 1999 [[Hope and Survival Happiness Group standoff]], which exposed the inadequacy of military-led internal security arrangements. The force operates under the [[Ministry of Interior (Balboa)|Ministry of Interior]] and is subject to the civil rights compliance requirements of the [[Twelve Guarantees]].

The [[International Cooperative Police Force]] (ICPF) is a joint AC-Balboan police force with authority throughout all of Balboa. It was established under the [[Twelve Guarantees]] to enforce the civil rights provisions and operates under AC command authority. The ICPF's mandate in the former mandate territory was phased out in the 1990s following compliance reviews, but its presence in the [[International City of Areza]] is perpetual.

== Local government ==

{{main|Administrative divisions of Balboa}}

Balboa's administrative structure comprises four levels of government. Every citizen resides within a province, a comarca, and a municipalitat; the ciutat and districte levels exist only in certain urban areas.

=== Provinces ===

Balboa is divided into five provinces — [[Tramuntana Province|Tramuntana]], [[Nurra Province|Nurra]], [[Jala Province|Jala]], [[Estret Province|Estret]], and [[Migjorn Province|Migjorn]] — each with an elected provincial assembly and a directly elected governor. The governor serves as the chief executive of the province and is responsible for provincial administration, infrastructure, and the coordination of comarca-level services. Provincial assemblies are elected by STV every four years and have legislative authority over matters devolved to the provinces by the national constitution, including education, health, and provincial transport.

