The [[International City of Areza]], within Estret Province, is a permanently neutral international territory governed under the [[Treaty of Areza]] (1973) and is not subject to Balboan sovereignty.

=== Comarcas ===

Each province is subdivided into [[comarca]]s, which serve as the principal intermediate level of government between the province and the municipalitat. Each comarca is headed by a directly elected commissioner ({{lang|ca|comissari}}), who serves as the chief executive and coordinates comarca-level services including regional planning, comarca roads, and the administration of comarca-wide facilities such as hospitals and secondary schools. Each comarca also has an elected comarca assembly ({{lang|ca|assemblea comarcal}}), whose members are elected by STV from population-proportional constituencies within the comarca every four years.

=== Municipalitats ===

The municipalitat (municipality) is the basic unit of local government. Each municipalitat is headed by a directly elected mayor ({{lang|ca|alcalde}}), who serves as the chief executive. Municipalitats are responsible for local services including water, waste management, local roads, primary education, and urban planning. Municipal councils ({{lang|ca|consell municipal}}) are elected by STV every four years.

=== Ciutats and districtes ===

In larger urban areas, an additional layer of sub-municipal government exists. Most cities with a population over 100,000 are divided into '''districtes''' (districts), each electing a representative to the city council. [[Sant Cristòfor]] is the only city in Balboa to operate a '''ciutat–districte''' system, in which the mainland municipalitat is divided into multiple ciutats, each with its own elected city council, and each ciutat is further subdivided into districtes.

== Constitutional framework ==

{{main|Constitution of Balboa|Twelve Guarantees}}

The Constitution of Balboa was adopted in 1974, following the country's reunification under the [[Treaty of Areza]] (1973). The constitution establishes the structure of government, the separation of powers, and the fundamental rights of citizens. It incorporates the [[Twelve Guarantees]] as entrenched provisions that cannot be amended or repealed without the consent of the [[Adonian Community]], ensuring that the civil rights and anti-discrimination protections established under the AC mandate period remain permanently safeguarded.

The constitution provides for:

* A directly elected president as head of state and head of government, with a maximum of two consecutive five-year terms
* A unicameral National Assembly with staggered elections
* An independent judiciary with a Constitutional Court and Supreme Court
* Devolved provincial government with elected assemblies and governors
* The Twelve Guarantees as entrenched constitutional provisions
* AC oversight of Guarantees enforcement through the AC Tribunal

Amendments to the constitution require a two-thirds majority of the National Assembly and the approval of the president. Amendments affecting the Twelve Guarantees additionally require the consent of the Adonian Community, as provided under the Twelfth Guarantee.

